<PageLayout lang="en" title="Privacy Policy" description="Fincanla privacy policy: what data is collected, how cookies and advertising partners are used, and what your rights are as a reader." alternates={staticPages.privacy}>
  <p><em>The site owner is based in Germany, so the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) applies. The legally binding version is the <a href={staticPages.privacy.de}>German privacy policy</a>.</em></p>
  <h2>Controller</h2>
  <p>The controller is the site owner named in the <a href={staticPages.imprint.en}>imprint</a>.</p>
  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>The site is delivered via Cloudflare. Technically necessary data (IP address, date, requested page, browser type) is processed to serve the site securely.</p>
  <h2>Data we collect</h2>
  <p>Fincanla has no accounts. Visit statistics may be measured anonymously.</p>
  <h2>Reader photos (community)</h2>
  <p>When you send a photo through the "Share your photo" form, we store the photo, the name (or nickname) you enter and the optional title and note, so we can review your submission and, if approved, publish it in the gallery. The legal basis is your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR). To limit abuse, we briefly keep only a one-way hash of your IP address, not the IP address itself. We use Cloudflare Turnstile to block automated submissions. Data is stored on Cloudflare's infrastructure.</p>
  <p>For rejected or removed submissions, the photo and personal details are deleted; only the status and reason remain. You can withdraw your consent and ask for your photo to be removed at any time – just email the address in the imprint.</p>
  <h2>Advertising (Google AdSense) and cookies</h2>
  <p>To cover the costs of this site we show ads through Google AdSense, provided by Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland. Google may use cookies and similar technologies to serve and measure ads; this can involve processing your IP address and browser data, including transfers to the USA (EU-US Data Privacy Framework).</p>
  <p>Personalised ads and the cookies they need are only used with your explicit consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR, § 25 TDDDG). You give or refuse consent in Google's consent window, which appears on your first visit, and you can change your choice at any time via the <strong>"Cookie settings"</strong> link at the bottom of every page. Without consent, Google shows at most limited, non-personalised ads.</p>
  <p>More information: <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads?hl=en" rel="noopener">How Google uses data in advertising</a>.</p>
  <p>We do not use analytics cookies.</p>
  <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
  <p>When you click an affiliate link, the store may set its own cookie to attribute the sale to us.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Contact details are in the <a href={staticPages.imprint.en}>imprint</a>. You have the right to access, correct and delete your data.</p>
</PageLayout>
